LocalAI admission ordering for paged serving.

Orders waiting requests by class (request priority, with aging), then fewest
uncached prompt tokens, then arrival, with an overtake cap: in the deferred
queue, at the pool admission wait and in the prompt fill of each step.
Also a per-request prefill cap, least-recently-used idle-slot eviction that
saves the slot to the RAM prompt cache and trims cells tail-first, and lazy
idle-slot saving under paged serving. The policy is in serving_policy.h.
Every hook runs only when common_params::paged_serving (and paged_order or
prefill_cap) is set. See backend/cpp/llama-cpp/PATCHES.md.

